      ],
      "captionArtboard": "four takes explored on the same artboard",
      "notes": "<p>This direction came out of the pixel/checkerboard doodles scattered across the first sketch page — building the letterform out of a small grid rather than one continuous stroke.</p><p>The same Illustrator artboard held several passes at the idea — the icon alone, the icon paired with the wordmark, and two translucent, gradient-blended takes that trade the hard pixel grid for something softer.</p><p>The animation tests a \"still loading\" behavior: pixel cells flicker at slightly different rates, like the mark is assembling itself, while the two bowls breathe gently so it never feels static.</p>",
